{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "1ae03117-de88-47e4-af92-e0212003c311",
    "name": "EMS Reinigungsservice - Mobile API",
    "description": "The endpoints the field-crew mobile app calls, in the order it calls them.\n\nHOW TO RUN\n1. Set the `base_url` variable (default http://localhost:8000).\n2. Set `email` / `password` to a Vorarbeiter or Administrator account.\n3. Send any request. The collection pre-request script logs in automatically and\n   stores the Sanctum token in `{{token}}`, so you never paste a token by hand.\n\nMANUAL VARIABLES\n`{{order_id}}`, `{{execution_id}}`, `{{location_id}}` and `{{complaint_id}}`\ndefault to 1. Fill them in from a real response, or let the Collection Runner\nsave the value to the environment after running the request that creates it.\n\nFOLDER ORDER\n1 sign in -> 2 read the day's work -> 3 run the execution workflow -> 4 report\ndamage -> 5 travel, notifications, reports. 3.10 closes the job and will not\nsucceed until the steps before it are done.\n\nCONTRACT NOTES\n- The photo endpoint takes `stage=before|after` and stores PATHS/URLs, not\n  file bodies. The app uploads to storage first and sends the URLs.\n- `key_returned` is only enforced when the site has `has_key_safe`, and\n  `alarm_activated` only when it has `has_alarm_system`.\n- If the shift was started with GPS, the closing call MUST send\n  `gps_work_end_lat` / `gps_work_end_lng` or it returns 422.\n- Financial fields (`price`, `internal_cost`, `profitability`, `revenue`,\n  `hourly_cost`) are never part of a field-crew response.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
